{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T04:12:07Z","thinking":"Exclude the requested indicators (ATR, SuperTrend, EMA Trailing, and Parabolic SAR) as per user feedback, acknowledging their common use and user's past negative experience with them getting stopped out.\n\n\nThe intuition is spot on; retail indicators are indeed stop-hunt magnets. Remove those from the TODO lists; we're going for smarter trailing methods. Now, let's explore advanced trailing approaches that smart money utilizes, starting with order flow and delta imbalances. I'll get those unconventional methods documented!\n\n\nOrder flow analysis reveals insights into buying and selling pressure; a positive delta suggests holding, but a significant negative delta (absorption cluster) indicates an aggressive seller and triggers stop adjustment. Candle body trailing ignores wicks, setting stops at body close levels to filter out market maker stop-hunts. Utilizing Fair Value Gaps (FVG) and imbalances provides stop-loss placements beyond the last unfilled FVG boundary.\n\n\nTick speed analysis detects impulse decay; a sharp deceleration after peak volume triggers a tight stop adjustment. A virtual stop-loss mechanism keeps the stop level internal, only executing a market order upon a breach in the order flow. Dynamic trailing utilizes a regression channel; the stop trails along the lower boundary (OLS - 2 sigma).\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"[Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8\nGet-Content \"Y:\\STRG\\TODO_STRG.md\" | Select-Object -Last 25","Cwd":"Y:\\STRG","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking last lines of TODO_STRG.md","toolSummary":"Read tail of TODO_STRG.md"}}]}
